course: dictionary
lesson: 15117
title: How salty is it?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Salinity tells you how salty water or soil is. It means how much salt is dissolved in it. Dissolved means the salt has mixed in so well that you cannot see it, but it still makes the water taste salty.
explain: «The sea has high salinity, so the water tastes very salty.» «The river has low salinity, so the water is almost fresh.» High salinity means lots of salt. Low salinity means only a little. Scientists can measure salinity by checking how much salt is in a set amount of water.
explain: Salinity matters on land too. «The farmer's field has high salinity, so the wheat will not grow.» Too much salt in soil makes it hard for plants to take in water. Salinity is measured the same way for soil and for water: by the amount of salt.
fact: Salinity means how much salt is dissolved in water or soil.
fact: Salinity is measured as grams of salt in one litre of water, or as parts per thousand.
fact: Seawater has a salinity of about 35 grams of salt per litre.
fact: The Dead Sea has very high salinity, so you float easily in it.
fact: Some fish live only in fresh water and some live only in the sea, because salinity is very different in each.
exercise: What does salinity mean? | How many fish live in it | *How much salt is dissolved in water or soil | How warm the water is | How deep the water is
exercise: «The river has low salinity.» Which is true about this river? | It has no water in it | It is the saltiest water on Earth | It has so much salt you can see it | *It has only a little salt in its water
exercise: Which place has the highest salinity? | A fresh mountain stream | A small pond in a park | Rain falling on a roof | *The Dead Sea
test: Ali says salinity is the same as temperature. Which is the correct meaning? | Salinity is how hot water is | Salinity is how far water flows each day | *Salinity is how much salt is in water or soil | Salinity is how many waves hit the shore
test: «Seawater has a salinity of about 35 grams per litre.» What does this number tell you? | *The grams of salt in one litre of seawater | How deep the sea is | How many litres of sea there are | How old the sea is
exam: What is the effect of high salinity in soil? | Plants grow faster, because salt is food | Salty soil is too heavy to dig | *Plants struggle to take in water from very salty soil | Salty soil is always too cold for plants
